      "text": "To solve the expression \\(\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}\\), we can use the difference of squares formula, which states \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\). Here, \\(a = 235\\) and \\(b = 221\\).\n\nSo, we can rewrite the expression as:\n\\[\n\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14} = \\frac{(235 - 221)(235 + 221)}{14}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the values \\(235 - 221\\) and \\(235 + 221\\):\n\\[\n235 - 221 = 14\n\\]\n\\[\n235 + 221 = 456\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these values back into the expression, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{(235 - 221)(235 + 221)}{14} = \\frac{14 \\cdot 456}{14}\n\\]\n\nThe \\(14\\) in the numerator and the \\(14\\) in the denominator cancel each other out:\n\\[\n\\frac{14 \\cdot 456}{14} = 456\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{456}\n\\]",
