      "text": "To find the value of \\(\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}\\), we will use the difference of squares formula, which is \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\). Here, \\(a = 235\\) and \\(b = 221\\).\n\nFirst, we apply the difference of squares formula:\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = (235 - 221)(235 + 221)\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate each term inside the parentheses:\n\\[\n235 - 221 = 14\n\\]\n\\[\n235 + 221 = 456\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute these values back into the expression:\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = 14 \\times 456\n\\]\n\nThen, we compute the product:\n\\[\n14 \\times 456 = 14 \\times (450 + 6) = 14 \\times 450 + 14 \\times 6 = 6300 + 84 = 6384\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = 6384\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to divide this result by 14:\n\\[\n\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14} = \\frac{6384}{14}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we perform the division:\n\\[\n\\frac{6384}{14} = 456\n\\]\n\nThus, the value is \\(\\boxed{456}\\).",
